The shipped CLI rendered `distinct method(s): .` on an Objective-C file whose
only fs_write reach was an untypable receiver: the disclosure fired, counted
the site correctly, and could not say WHICH method -- most of its value.

NOT A NEW DESIGN. ADR-0036 Ruling 1 already made the id's name slot
deliberately lossy and said why -- "the ID is a location-addressed key, not a
fidelity surface -- full-fidelity names live in Symbol.name ... Consumers that
need the exact name MUST read Symbol.name, never re-derive it from the ID" --
and the ADR's own amendment lists the producer-side sanitisation as a deferred
follow-up. This is that follow-up coming due.

THE DEFECT WAS THE UNFILLED HOME, NOT THE COLON. Measured on a 14-line repro:
node.name '', qualified_name None, dst_ref None -- writeToFile:atomically:
existed NOWHERE in the output. The boundary node is synthesised FROM the id,
which made the id the name's only home, the one arrangement Ruling 1 forbids.
An objc selector ENDS in a colon, so parts[-2] is the EMPTY STRING and every
such selector collapsed onto one node.

  1. meta['callee_name'] registered on the edge-meta axis (ADR-0024),
     single_writer, stamped UNCONDITIONALLY by make_unresolved_edge -- the one
     factory all 57 unresolved-external sites across 36 analyzers use.
     Unconditional because WI-huzuv correctly withholds dst_ref when the module
     is unknown (precisely the objc cell), and a name living in dst_ref
     sometimes and meta otherwise is one fact with two homes.
  2. create_boundary_nodes prefers that home over the lossy slot.
  3. Both disclosure sites read it through ONE helper; they are a pair
     (_site_method parses _call_site_label back out).
  4. _canonical_external_id folds ':' -> '.' for the ID while Symbol.name keeps
     full fidelity.

ITEM 4 IS A REGRESSION I INTRODUCED AND THE VALIDATOR CAUGHT. The first cut fed
the lossless name into the minted id -- rust:external:0-0:Vec::with_capacity:...
-- which id_format rejects (double_colon_separator, INV-sadiv); bellman went
1 -> 16 violations. Getting the lossless half right by breaking the lossy half
is not getting Ruling 1 right. Shipped state: bellman at 0, clearing the one
violation that pre-dated this work.

A SECOND LANGUAGE, found on a repo meant only as a non-destruction control:
parts[-2] discarded the receiver type on every Rust Type::method call, so
bellman's 13 truncated boundary nodes become 16 qualified ones --
batch_normalize splits back into E::G1::batch_normalize and
E::G2::batch_normalize. objc is where the same defect produced an EMPTY name
rather than a truncated one.

MEASURED AT THREE LAYERS. Mantle, one survey scored both ways: distinct callee
names 19 -> 82, dsts with an empty name 179/229 -> 0, nameless boundary nodes 0.
Published CLI: "distinct method(s): ." -> "distinct method(s):
writeToFile:atomically:". NO VERDICT FLIPPED on either repo -- this is identity
and disclosure quality, not coverage. Mantle's figures are close to but not an
exact reproduction of the item's filed 80/17.

